      "section": "opening",
      "slot": "opening",
      "text": "Aspose.Slides FOSS for Python reads and writes PowerPoint .pptx presentations. It creates, reads, and edits presentations by modeling them as Presentation, Slide, Shape, and TextFrame objects, with no Microsoft Office installation or COM interop required. It supports adding shapes, tables, connectors, images, charts, text formatting, slide transitions, and document properties."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:002",
        "format:input.pptx",
        "format:output.pptx",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.slidecollection.add_clone",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.slidecollection.add_empty_slide",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.slidecollection.remove_at"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:1",
      "text": "It creates new presentations and edits existing ones by adding empty slides with add_empty_slide, cloning slides with add_clone, and removing slides at specific indices with remove_at, always saving to .pptx format."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:003",
        "example:005",
        "example:006",
        "example:007",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.shapecollection.add_auto_shape",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.shapecollection.add_connector",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.shapecollection.add_table"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:2",
      "text": "It adds auto shapes such as rectangles and circles, tables with configurable rows and columns, and connectors like bent connectors to link shapes, all through the ShapeCollection methods add_auto_shape, add_table, and add_connector."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:004",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.baseportionformat.font_bold",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.baseportionformat.font_height",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.nullablebool",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.paragraphformat.bullet"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:3",
      "text": "It formats text at the portion level with font_height and font_bold, and at the paragraph level with bullet formatting, using NullableBool to represent tri-state boolean values for properties like font_bold."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:012",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.charts.chartdataworkbook",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.charts.chartseries",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.charts.charttype"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:4",
      "text": "It creates charts of types like ClusteredColumn through ChartType, binds data via an embedded ChartDataWorkbook, and populates ChartSeries with data points for bars, columns, and other chart elements."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:013",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.animation.sequence",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.slideshow.morphtransition",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.slideshow.transitiontype"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:5",
      "text": "It applies slide transitions such as Circle using TransitionType, configures MorphTransition effects, and manages animation sequences with Sequence to control timing and effect ordering."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:008",
        "format:input.png",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.imagecollection.add_image",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.images.from_file",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.images.from_stream"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:6",
      "text": "It embeds images from files or streams using Images.from_file and Images.from_stream, and adds them to slides as picture frames via ImageCollection.add_image."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:011",
        "public_symbol:slides_foss.documentproperties.author",
